1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,523
The Clever Monkey and the Greedy Crocodile
A Jungle Adventure Full of Tricks and Laughter

2
00:00:07,023 --> 00:00:12,076
Once upon a time, there lived a clever little monkey
in a beautiful tropical jungle.

3
00:00:12,576 --> 00:00:18,973
One day, the monkey wanted to cross a wide river.
But the river was very deep, and the water flowed strongly.

4
00:00:19,173 --> 00:00:23,139
There were no trees nearby,
so he couldn't jump from one tree to another.

5
00:00:23,639 --> 00:00:28,991
The monkey sat on the riverbank, scratching his head
and wondering how he could get to the other side.

6
00:00:29,291 --> 00:00:31,827
"Oh dear! How am I going to cross this river?"

7
00:00:32,327 --> 00:00:35,076
Suddenly, a crocodile appeared from the water.

8
00:00:35,576 --> 00:00:39,989
"Hello, my little friend!
Why are you sitting here looking so sad?"

9
00:00:40,289 --> 00:00:42,804
"I want to cross the river, but I don't know how!"

10
00:00:43,204 --> 00:00:47,831
"That's easy! Climb onto my back.
I'll carry you safely across the river."

11
00:00:48,131 --> 00:00:51,591
The monkey was delighted.
"Really? That's very kind of you!"

12
00:00:52,091 --> 00:00:57,400
The monkey happily climbed onto the crocodile's back,
and they started swimming across the river.

13
00:00:57,700 --> 00:01:00,065
But the crocodile had a secret plan.

14
00:01:00,565 --> 00:01:06,643
"Hehehe! Once we reach the middle of the river,
I'll dive underwater and make this little monkey my dinner!"

15
00:01:07,143 --> 00:01:10,191
Everything seemed fine as they swam through the water.

16
00:01:10,691 --> 00:01:15,765
But when they reached the middle of the river,
the crocodile suddenly began to dive underwater.

17
00:01:16,265 --> 00:01:19,192
"Hey! Hey! What are you doing?" shouted the monkey.

18
00:01:19,692 --> 00:01:25,840
The crocodile didn't say a word.
Instead, he thought: "You fool! Don't you know I'm going to eat you?"

19
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:32,631
The monkey was terrified. He suddenly realized the danger
and knew he had to think quickly to save himself.

20
00:01:33,131 --> 00:01:35,581
Suddenly, an idea came to his mind.

21
00:01:36,081 --> 00:01:38,381
"Wait! Wait! My friend!"

22
00:01:39,181 --> 00:01:44,043
"Oh, I almost forgot! I want to bring my auntie with me.
She's waiting on the riverbank."

23
00:01:44,343 --> 00:01:49,055
"She's very fat and much bigger than me.
She's too heavy to walk, so she needs a ride."

24
00:01:49,455 --> 00:01:53,271
"I'm just a skinny little monkey,
but my auntie is a much bigger meal!"

25
00:01:53,771 --> 00:02:00,388
The greedy crocodile started thinking:
"Hmm! If I take him back, I can get two monkeys instead of one!"

26
00:02:00,888 --> 00:02:05,173
"And if his auntie is really that fat,
I'll have a much bigger meal!"

27
00:02:05,673 --> 00:02:09,788
"That's a wonderful idea!
Let's go back and get your auntie!"

28
00:02:10,188 --> 00:02:14,388
The crocodile quickly turned around
and swam back towards the riverbank.

29
00:02:14,888 --> 00:02:20,539
As soon as they reached the shore, the clever monkey jumped off
and quickly climbed up a nearby tree.

30
00:02:21,039 --> 00:02:24,343
Then he looked down at the crocodile
and burst out laughing.

31
00:02:24,843 --> 00:02:30,067
"Ha! Ha! Ha! Do you really think I'm a fool?
You tried to trick me, but I'm much cleverer than you!"

32
00:02:30,567 --> 00:02:35,456
The crocodile looked up in surprise.
"Hey! Come back! Where is your auntie?"

33
00:02:35,956 --> 00:02:39,629
The monkey laughed even louder.
"My auntie? She's safe at home!"

34
00:02:39,929 --> 00:02:42,129
"And you can forget about your dinner!"

35
00:02:42,629 --> 00:02:46,467
The crocodile floated sadly in the river,
with an empty stomach.

36
00:02:46,967 --> 00:02:51,017
The monkey sat comfortably on a tree branch,
enjoying his victory.

37
00:02:51,517 --> 00:02:54,352
"Next time, don't underestimate a clever monkey!"

38
00:02:54,852 --> 00:02:59,031
And that's how the clever little monkey
escaped from the greedy crocodile.

39
00:02:59,531 --> 00:03:06,568
The Moral of the Story:
Intelligence is more powerful than strength.
A clever mind can save you from any danger.

